-- title:
--   Transported specialisation is a reduction of places mod ℓ
-- statement:
--   Fix $N \ge 1$ and a prime $\ell$, and let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ whose residue field $\kappa = \mathrm{ResidueField}(A)$ has characteristic $\ell$, with $\ell \nmid N$. Let `fm` be a `FibreModel` for $N$, $A$, $\ell$ over $\kappa$ with reduction map the residue homomorphism of $A$: that is, a pair of subrings $B_{\mathrm{fin}}, B_{\inf}$ of the base-changed field $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} \cdot F_N^{\mathrm{full}} \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}})$ containing the constants from $A$, with $\bar\jmath, \bar\jmath_N \in B_{\mathrm{fin}}$ and $\bar\jmath^{-1} \in B_{\inf}$, each element integral over the respective affine base ring, together with ring homomorphisms $\pi_{\mathrm{fin}}, \pi_{\inf}$ into $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,\kappa\,N = \kappa(\tilde\jmath, \tilde\jmath_N)$ which reduce constants through the residue map and send $\bar\jmath, \bar\jmath_N, \bar\jmath^{-1}$ to their characteristic-$\ell$ counterparts. Let `cc` be a `CuspChart` for `fm`, namely the assertion that $\bar\jmath_N \bar\jmath^{-N} \in B_{\inf}$ and that $\pi_{\inf}$ sends it to $\tilde\jmath_N \tilde\jmath^{-N}$. Let `dataAll` assign to each divisor $d \mid N$ a `ModularPolynomialData`, i.e. a monic $\Phi \in \mathbb{Z}[X][Y]$ of degree $\psi(d)$ with $\Phi(j, j_d) = 0$ on $q$-expansions, and assume the image of $\Phi$ for $d = N$ over $\kappa$, viewed in $\mathrm{RatFunc}(\kappa)[Y]$, is separable. Finally assume $\kappa(\tilde\jmath, \tilde\jmath_N) = \mathrm{modularFunctionFieldFullC}\,\kappa\,N$, the subfield of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(\kappa)$ generated by all divisor expansions. The conclusion is that the map sending a place $P$ of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,N$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ to the place obtained from $\mathrm{spPlace}$ of `fm` (built from the surjectivity of the residue map, `dataAll` and the separability hypothesis) by transporting it along the ring isomorphism induced by that equality of subfields — the transport `Place.congrRingEquiv`, which pulls the valuation subring back along the inverse isomorphism — satisfies [`ModularCurve.IsPlaceReductionModL A N`](def/ModularCurve_ReductionModL.html#L179), i.e. the predicate `IsPlaceReductionAlong` for $A$, the residue map of $A$ and $N$.
--
--   This identifies the specialisation map attached to a fibre model of $X_0(N)$ at a place of residue characteristic $\ell \nmid N$, read on the full special-fibre function field through the stated equality of subfields, as a reduction of places in Deuring's sense. It is used to compare the constructed specialisation with the canonical reduction map, and feeds the construction of smooth proper models and of the finite maps to the Igusa curve.
